  "compiled": "2026-09-12",
  "method": "MakerWorld design 2168356 (SnapLock V3, Hugo) and its predecessors and remixes were read through MakerWorld's public design API because the HTML pages sit behind a Cloudflare challenge; model downloads require a login and were not obtained. The designer's SnapLock V3.f3d, supplied by the user, is a zip with Zstandard (method 93) members; its ASM BREP blobs were read at token level to extract vertex and plane extents of the final bodies and the design stream was searched for parameter expressions. Feature roles (catch bar, pivot boss, tongue, skirt) are inferred from the design pictures. Full page archive, images, scripts and findings.md stay in var/research/snaplock/ (local, not committed).",
  "licence": "SnapLock V3, V1, V2 and the Thin Remix carry the MakerWorld Exclusive License: derivatives only on MakerWorld with attribution, no re-hosting, commercial use prohibited. The article describes the mechanism and quotes extents as a reviewed example; no SnapLock geometry, image or file is redistributed in this repository.",
